oc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine\/number","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwavyline\/number"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWavyLine":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLWavyLine","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWavyLine","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wavy lines are one way to indicate trills and vibrato. When used with a barline element, they should always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have "},{"code":"type=\"continue\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set. The smufl attribute specifies a particular wavy line glyph from the SMuFL Multi-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment lines range."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLWavyLine"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLWavyLine"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwavyline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"title":"MXLNumberLevel","abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}